# TypeScript style

- Doc-comment every function, method, and named/assigned callback: purpose, non-obvious inputs/outputs, side effects, failures. Restating the name is not enough.
- Prefer explicit types at module boundaries; match neighboring import style (`.ts` extensions in local imports where already used).
- No drive-by refactors or unrelated formatting. Run `pnpm exec vp check` on touched packages.
- Tests colocated under package `tests/`; use `vite-plus/test` (`describe`/`expect`/`test`).
- Errors: protocol → `ProtocolError` with field paths; extension git → `GitError`; UI surfaces via `showError`.
